# JSDoc — Common Components (Warn)

Apply when touching files under `src/components/common/**`. Document **new or modified** exports only.

## Required

- Exported component function — one-line summary above the component
- Exported props interfaces — per-prop `/** */` on non-obvious fields (match `DiyVerificationScreenView.tsx`)
- Exported utility functions co-located in common components (e.g. `*Util.ts`, `*.utils.ts`)

## Not required

- Private styled components, inline handlers, or internal subcomponents
- Obvious props where the name and type are self-explanatory (e.g. `disabled: boolean`)
- Journey screens under `src/components/Screens/**` (out of scope)

## Examples

```typescript
export interface NPSelectProps {
  /** Label shown above the select field. */
  label: string;
  /** Called when the selected option changes. */
  onChange: (value: string) => void;
  options: Option[];
}

/**
 * Renders a styled MUI select with project-standard error display.
 */
export const NPSelect = ({ label, onChange, options }: NPSelectProps) => { ... };
```

## Pattern

- Prefer prop-level JSDoc on the interface over repeating `@param` on the component when props are a single object
- Keep summaries action-oriented: what the component renders or does, not implementation details
